\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:902:             (raise-exit (assoc {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding}\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:912:                   (raise-exit (assoc {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown}\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1044:                 (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1731:     ;; the key `[]` writes to, or the engine's occupied-slot error\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2282:                                      {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2388:                           (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason)\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2396:                                (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason)\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4316:                               (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"The paths already differ: Python installs a per-call exception bridge, while JavaScript and PHP entries run the body without connecting source exceptions to the caller’s raise exit. Clojure uses private outcome vectors internally and converts errors at the public entry. I’m checking foreign-condition reception, rethrow behavior, and test coverage next.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '1,280p'; nl -ba test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj | sed -n '1,280p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba test/yang/call/conformance.clj | sed -n '1,280p'; nl -ba test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj | sed -n '1,280p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     1\\t(ns yang.call.conformance\\n     2\\t  \\\"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\\n     3\\t   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\\n     4\\t   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\t   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\\n     7\\t   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\\n     8\\t   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\\n     9\\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`, `py/run-main`,\\n    10\\t   `clj/run-main`), reads each named export from the donor runtime's global\\n    11\\t   namespace, and projects it into the caller runtime's namespace under the\\n    12\\t   same name; then the caller source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own\\n    13\\t   entry. The composition is a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is\\n    14\\t   rewritten, no foreign `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is\\n    15\\t   inserted, and the projected value is the donor's own callable value\\n    16\\t   (identity survives).\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\\n    19\\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\\n    20\\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\\n    21\\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\\n    24\\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\\n    25\\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php`, `py` and `clj` are\\n    26\\t   published beside them. The AST walker is not a backend: its links are\\n    27\\t   refused until L-b.\\\"\\n    28\\t  (:require\\n    29\\t    [clojure.string :as str]\\n    30\\t    [yang.clojure :as clj-comp]\\n    31\\t    [yang.clojure.prelude :as clj-prelude]\\n    32\\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\\n    33\\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\\n    34\\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\\n    35\\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\\n    36\\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\\n    37\\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\\n    38\\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\\n    39\\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\\n    40\\t    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\\n    41\\t    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\\n    42\\t    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\\n    43\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\\n    44\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\\n    45\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\\n    46\\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\\n    47\\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t(def ^:private published-php\\n    51\\t  \\\"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\\n    52\\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\\\"\\n    53\\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\n    54\\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\n    55\\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t(def ^:private published-py\\n    59\\t  \\\"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\\n    60\\t   `yang.call` revision.\\\"\\n    61\\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\n    62\\t           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\n    63\\t                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\\n    64\\t\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t(def ^:private published-clj\\n    67\\t  \\\"`clj` published beside `js`, `php` and `py`, over the same host registry\\n    68\\t   and `yang.call` revision.\\\"\\n    69\\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\\n    70\\t           (clj-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\\n    71\\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\\n    72\\t\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\t(defn- parse-ok\\n    75\\t  \\\"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\\\"\\n    76\\t  [parse source]\\n    77\\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\\n    78\\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\\n    79\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"donor or caller source does not parse\\\"\\n    80\\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\\n    81\\t    pk))\\n    82\\t\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\t(defn- python-export-symbol\\n    85\\t  [export]\\n    86\\t  (symbol (str \\\"xlang.python.export.\\\" export)))\\n    87\\t\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t(defn- python-unit\\n    90\\t  [packet exports]\\n    91\\t  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\\n    92\\t         (u/seq-nodes\\n    93\\t           (concat (map (fn [export]\\n    94\\t                          (u/sexp->uast\\n    95\\t                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\\n    96\\t                                  {:py/str export} (python-export-symbol export))))\\n    97\\t                        exports)\\n    98\\t                   [(py-lower/lower-module-body packet)]))))\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t\\n   101\\t(def frontends\\n   102\\t  \\\"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\\n   103\\t\\n   104\\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\\n   105\\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\\n   106\\t   - `:deps` (optional): pinned requirements beyond the runtime its\\n   107\\t     lowered units read directly (the clojure unit's `yang.call` reads);\\n   108\\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\\n   109\\t   - `:unit`: packet and projected exports to the lowered unit its\\n   110\\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\\n   111\\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\\n   112\\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table, Python's main\\n   113\\t     module dictionary, the clojure runtime's task-local namespace cell);\\n   114\\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\\n   115\\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name;\\n   116\\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\\\"\\n   117\\t  {:typescript\\n   118\\t   {:runtime 'js,\\n   119\\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\\n   120\\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\\n   121\\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\\n   122\\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit packet))),\\n   123\\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\\n   124\\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\\n   125\\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\\n   126\\t    :render render/output},\\n   127\\t   :php\\n   128\\t   {:runtime 'php,\\n   129\\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\\n   130\\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\\n   131\\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\\n   132\\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body packet))),\\n   133\\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\\n   134\\t    :read-export (fn [export]\\n   135\\t                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\\n   136\\t    :project (fn [name value]\\n   137\\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\\n   138\\t    :render php-h/render},\\n   139\\t   :python\\n   140\\t   {:runtime 'py,\\n   141\\t    :address #(:address @published-py),\\n   142\\t    :refusal [:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free],\\n   143\\t    :parse #(parse-ok py-parser/parse-source %),\\n   144\\t    :unit python-unit,\\n   145\\t    :run-main 'py/run-main,\\n   146\\t    :read-export (fn [export]\\n   147\\t                   (list 'py/global-get\\n   148\\t                         (list 'py/module-dict\\n   149\\t                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \\\"__main__\\\"}))\\n   150\\t                         {:py/str export})),\\n   151\\t    :project (fn [name value]\\n   152\\t               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\\n   153\\t    :render py-render/output},\\n   154\\t   :clojure\\n   155\\t   {:runtime 'clj,\\n   156\\t    :address #(:address @published-clj),\\n   157\\t    :refusal [:yang.clojure/refusal :yang.clojure/undeclared-free],\\n   158\\t    :deps (fn [] {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published)}),\\n   159\\t    :parse clj-comp/read-forms,\\n   160\\t    :unit (fn [packet exports] (clj-comp/lower-unit packet exports)),\\n   161\\t    :run-main 'clj/run-main,\\n   162\\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'clj/global-get export)),\\n   163\\t    :project (fn [name value]\\n   164\\t               ;; The runtime global namespace is the one binding (as\\n   165\\t               ;; `js/define-global!` is for a JS caller): `lower-unit`\\n   166\\t               ;; reads each projected name through `clj/global-get`, so\\n   167\\t               ;; no task-store binding duplicates it. A caller top-level\\n   168\\t               ;; definition of the same name publishes after the\\n   169\\t               ;; projection and shadows it.\\n   170\\t               (list 'clj/define-global! name value)),\\n   171\\t    :render clj-comp/output}})\\n   172\\t\\n   173\\t\\n   174\\t(defn- profile\\n   175\\t  [frontend]\\n   176\\t  (or (get frontends frontend)\\n   177\\t      (throw (ex-info \\\"frontend not admitted\\\" {:frontend frontend}))))\\n   178\\t\\n   179\\t\\n   180\\t(defn- modules\\n   181\\t  \\\"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it,\\n   182\\t   with the clojure guest library's host surface installed beside them.\\n   183\\t   Donor publication declares free names over this same registry, so a\\n   184\\t   clojure donor using the guest library (its `kind` and `portable`\\n   185\\t   hosts) publishes like it runs.\\\"\\n   186\\t  []\\n   187\\t  (clj-prelude/admit (php-prelude/admit (h/registry))))\\n   188\\t\\n   189\\t\\n   190\\t(defn publish-donor!\\n   191\\t  \\\"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\\n   192\\t   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\\n   193\\t   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\\\"\\n   194\\t  ([frontend source]\\n   195\\t   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \\\"xlang.donor.\\\" (name frontend)))))\\n   196\\t  ([frontend source module]\\n   197\\t   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit deps]} (profile frontend)\\n   198\\t         [refusal-key reason] refusal\\n   199\\t         spec (core-module/module-spec\\n   200\\t                refusal-key reason (modules)\\n   201\\t                {:name module,\\n   202\\t                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\\n   203\\t                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\\n   204\\t                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))]),\\n   205\\t                 :exports '#{body},\\n   206\\t                 :runtime-name runtime,\\n   207\\t                 :runtime-address (address),\\n   208\\t                 :deps (if deps (deps) {})})\\n   209\\t         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\\n   210\\t     {:frontend frontend,\\n   211\\t      :module module,\\n   212\\t      :address (:address result),\\n   213\\t      :links (:links result)})))\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t\\n   216\\t(defn- runtime-entry\\n   217\\t  \\\"Require and initialize each distinct runtime of `frontend-keys`, once.\\\"\\n   218\\t  [frontend-keys]\\n   219\\t  (into [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)]\\n   220\\t        (mapcat (fn [runtime]\\n   221\\t                  [(core-module/require-node runtime)\\n   222\\t                   (u/sexp->uast (list (symbol (str runtime) \\\"init!\\\")))]))\\n   223\\t        (distinct (map (comp :runtime profile) frontend-keys))))\\n   224\\t\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t(defn- donor-run\\n   227\\t  \\\"The donor module required and its body run under its runtime's entry.\\\"\\n   228\\t  [{:keys [frontend module]}]\\n   229\\t  [(core-module/require-node module)\\n   230\\t   (u/app (u/v (:run-main (profile frontend)))\\n   231\\t          (u/v (symbol (str module) \\\"body\\\")))])\\n   232\\t\\n   233\\t\\n   234\\t(defn export-program\\n   235\\t  \\\"The program whose value is the donor's `export`, read from its runtime's\\n   236\\t   global namespace after its body ran.\\\"\\n   237\\t  [donor export]\\n   238\\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))]\\n   239\\t    (u/mark-tails\\n   240\\t      (u/seq-nodes (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor)])\\n   241\\t                           (donor-run donor)\\n   242\\t                           [(u/sexp->uast (read-export export))])))))\\n   243\\t\\n   244\\t\\n   245\\t(defn compose\\n   246\\t  \\\"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\\n   247\\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\\n   248\\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\\n   249\\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\\\"\\n   250\\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\\n   251\\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\\n   252\\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\\n   253\\t    (u/mark-tails\\n   254\\t      (u/seq-nodes\\n   255\\t        (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor) caller-frontend])\\n   256\\t                (donor-run donor)\\n   257\\t                (map (fn [export]\\n   258\\t                       (let [value (symbol (str \\\"xlang.export.\\\" export))]\\n   259\\t                         (u/let1 value\\n   260\\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (read-export export))\\n   261\\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (project export value)))))\\n   262\\t                     exports)\\n   263\\t                [(u/app (u/v run-main) (unit (parse caller-source) exports))])))))\\n   264\\t\\n   265\\t\\n   266\\t(defn link-source\\n   267\\t  \\\"The serving composition naming the runtimes and the donor module.\\\"\\n   268\\t  [{:keys [module address]}]\\n   269\\t  (h/source {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published),\\n   270\\t             'js (:address @h/published),\\n   271\\t             'php (:address @published-php),\\n   272\\t             'py (:address @published-py),\\n   273\\t             'clj (:address @published-clj),\\n   274\\t             module address}))\\n   275\\t\\n   276\\t\\n   277\\t(defn run-program\\n   278\\t  \\\"`{backend value}` of `ast`, linked against `donor`, on each vector VM.\\\"\\n   279\\t  [donor ast]\\n   280\\t  (let [src (link-source donor)]\\n     1\\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\\n     2\\t  \\\"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\\n     3\\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\\n     4\\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\\n     5\\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\\n     6\\t   task, one run.\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t   The seam is explicit published-export composition (8.10.11), owned by\\n     9\\t   `yang.call.conformance`: the donor source is published as a module and\\n    10\\t   run unmodified, its named export is read from the donor runtime's global\\n    11\\t   namespace (`globalThis.ts_fn`, PHP's `phpfn` function) and projected into the caller\\n    12\\t   runtime's namespace under the same name, and the caller source runs\\n    13\\t   unmodified. No call node is rewritten and no foreign `:code` extracted:\\n    14\\t   the caller holds the donor's own function cell, as the identity check\\n    15\\t   (`stored === phpfn`) shows.\\n    16\\t\\n    17\\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\\n    18\\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\\n    19\\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. Each case runs\\n    20\\t   linked on the three vector VMs, which must agree.\\\"\\n    21\\t  (:require\\n    22\\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n    23\\t    [yang.call.conformance :as xl]))\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\\n    27\\t  (testing \\\"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\\\"\\n    28\\t    (is (= \\\"4\\\"\\n    29\\t           (xl/call [:typescript \\\"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\\\"]\\n    30\\t                    [\\\"ts_fn\\\"]\\n    31\\t                    [:php \\\"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\\\"]))))\\n    32\\t  (testing \\\"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\\\"\\n    33\\t    (is (= \\\"yes\\\"\\n    34\\t           (xl/call [:typescript \\\"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\\\"]\\n    35\\t                    [\\\"ts_fn\\\"]\\n    36\\t                    [:php \\\"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\\\"])))))\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t\\n    39\\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\\n    40\\t  (testing \\\"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\\\"\\n    41\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"true 5\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n    42\\t           (xl/call [:php \\\"<?php function phpfn($a, $b) { return $a + $b; }\\\"]\\n    43\\t                    [\\\"phpfn\\\"]\\n    44\\t                    [:typescript\\n    45\\t                     \\\"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\\\"])))))\\n    46\\t\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t(deftest python-calls-typescript-closure-test\\n    49\\t  (testing \\\"TS stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\\\"\\n    50\\t    (is (= {:py/out [\\\"22\\\"], :py/exception nil}\\n    51\\t           (xl/call [:typescript\\n    52\\t                     (str \\\"globalThis.ts_apply = f => { globalThis.stored = f; \\\"\\n    53\\t                          \\\"return stored === f ? f(20n) + 1n : -1n; };\\\")]\\n    54\\t                    [\\\"ts_apply\\\"]\\n    55\\t                    [:python \\\"print(ts_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\\\\n\\\"])))))\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t(deftest typescript-calls-python-closure-test\\n    59\\t  (testing \\\"Python stores and calls the same TS function cell it received\\\"\\n    60\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"22n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n    61\\t           (xl/call [:python\\n    62\\t                     (str \\\"def py_apply(f):\\\\n\\\"\\n    63\\t                          \\\"    global stored\\\\n\\\"\\n    64\\t                          \\\"    stored = f\\\\n\\\"\\n    65\\t                          \\\"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\\\")]\\n    66\\t                    [\\\"py_apply\\\"]\\n    67\\t                    [:typescript\\n    68\\t                     \\\"console.log(py_apply(x => x + 1n));\\\"])))))\\n    69\\t\\n    70\\t\\n    71\\t(deftest python-calls-php-closure-test\\n    72\\t  (testing \\\"PHP stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\\\"\\n    73\\t    (is (= {:py/out [\\\"22\\\"], :py/exception nil}\\n    74\\t           (xl/call [:php\\n    75\\t                     (str \\\"<?php function php_apply($f) { global $stored; \\\"\\n    76\\t                          \\\"$stored = $f; return $stored === $f ? $f(20) + 1 : -1; }\\\")]\\n    77\\t                    [\\\"php_apply\\\"]\\n    78\\t                    [:python \\\"print(php_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\\\\n\\\"])))))\\n    79\\t\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t(deftest php-calls-python-closure-test\\n    82\\t  (testing \\\"Python stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\\\"\\n    83\\t    (is (= \\\"22\\\"\\n    84\\t           (xl/call [:python\\n    85\\t                     (str \\\"def py_apply(f):\\\\n\\\"\\n    86\\t                          \\\"    global stored\\\\n\\\"\\n    87\\t                          \\\"    stored = f\\\\n\\\"\\n    88\\t                          \\\"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\\\")]\\n    89\\t                    [\\\"py_apply\\\"]\\n    90\\t                    [:php \\\"<?php echo py_apply(function($x) { return $x + 1; });\\\"])))))\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\t;; yang.clojure <-> TypeScript, both directions. yang.clojure now publishes\\n    94\\t;; its runtime module (`clj`: the run-main entry, the task-local global\\n    95\\t;; namespace and the admission surface, yang.clojure.prelude), so the named\\n    96\\t;; skip is closed: the helper drives a clojure donor or caller like any\\n    97\\t;; other admitted frontend, and the same-cell identity check runs here too.\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t(deftest clojure-closure-called-from-typescript-test\\n   101\\t  (testing \\\"TS stores and calls the same clojure function cell it received\\\"\\n   102\\t    ;; Clojure integers are bare exact integers, the value JS spells as a\\n   103\\t    ;; BigInt, so the TS callback adds with `1n` and logs `22n`.\\n   104\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"true 22n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   105\\t           (xl/call [:clojure \\\"(defn clj_apply [f] (+ (f 20) 1))\\\"]\\n   106\\t                    [\\\"clj_apply\\\"]\\n   107\\t                    [:typescript\\n   108\\t                     (str \\\"const stored = clj_apply; \\\"\\n   109\\t                          \\\"console.log(stored === clj_apply, stored(x => x + 1n));\\\")])))))\\n   110\\t\\n   111\\t\\n   112\\t(deftest typescript-closure-called-from-clojure-test\\n   113\\t  (testing \\\"TS stores and calls the same clojure function cell it received\\\"\\n   114\\t    (is (= \\\"22\\\"\\n   115\\t           (xl/call [:typescript\\n   116\\t                     (str \\\"globalThis.ts_apply = f => { globalThis.stored = f; \\\"\\n   117\\t                          \\\"return stored === f ? f(20n) + 1n : -1n; };\\\")]\\n   118\\t                    [\\\"ts_apply\\\"]\\n   119\\t                    [:clojure \\\"(ts_apply (fn [x] (+ x 1)))\\\"])))))\\n   120\\t\\n   121\\t\\n   122\\t(deftest clojure-projection-through-runtime-globals-test\\n   123\\t  (testing \\\"the projected value is read via clj/global-get inside the caller's run\\\"\\n   124\\t    ;; `ts_apply` is no top-level definition of the caller, so its read\\n   125\\t    ;; inside `apply-it` reaches the runtime global namespace the helper\\n   126\\t    ;; projected into, not a task-store binding.\\n   127\\t    (is (= \\\"22\\\"\\n   128\\t           (xl/call [:typescript\\n   129\\t                     (str \\\"globalThis.ts_apply = f => { globalThis.stored = f; \\\"\\n   130\\t                          \\\"return stored === f ? f(20n) + 1n : -1n; };\\\")]\\n   131\\t                    [\\\"ts_apply\\\"]\\n   132\\t                    [:clojure\\n   133\\t                     \\\"(defn apply-it [] (ts_apply (fn [x] (+ x 1)))) (apply-it)\\\"]))))\\n   134\\t  (testing \\\"a second clj/run-main entry still sees the earlier unit's globals\\\"\\n   135\\t    (is (= \\\"42\\\"\\n   136\\t           (xl/call [:clojure \\\"(def answer 42)\\\"]\\n   137\\t                    [\\\"answer\\\"]\\n   138\\t                    [:clojure \\\"(defn get-answer [] answer) (get-answer)\\\"])))))\\n   139\\t\\n   140\\t\\n   141\\t(deftest clojure-caller-shadows-projected-global-test\\n   142\\t  (testing \\\"a caller-defined name shadows the projected one\\\"\\n   143\\t    ;; The caller's own `shared` runs: its definition publishes after the\\n   144\\t    ;; projection, so the runtime global holds the caller's function.\\n   145\\t    (is (= \\\"21\\\"\\n   146\\t           (xl/call [:clojure \\\"(defn shared [x] (+ x 100))\\\"]\\n   147\\t                    [\\\"shared\\\"]\\n   148\\t                    [:clojure \\\"(defn shared [x] (+ x 1)) (shared 20)\\\"])))))\\n   149\\t\\n   150\\t\\n   151\\t(deftest clojure-source-cell-ref-map-invocation-test\\n   152\\t  (testing \\\"a source map {:type :cell-ref} is ordinary invocable data\\\"\\n   153\\t    ;; The donor's exported function invokes its own source map literal:\\n   154\\t    ;; the map lookup answers 42, where the structural cell test used to\\n   155\\t    ;; dereference the map as a cell and fail the VM.\\n   156\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"42n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   157\\t           (xl/call [:clojure\\n   158\\t                     \\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :marker 42} :marker))\\\"]\\n   159\\t                    [\\\"probe\\\"]\\n   160\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(probe());\\\"]))))\\n   161\\t  (testing \\\"a source map with the full forged cell-ref shape is ordinary invocable data\\\"\\n   162\\t    ;; The map spells every key of an issued reference among its own\\n   163\\t    ;; entries; it is still data, so the lookup answers 42 where key\\n   164\\t    ;; presence alone used to dereference it and fail the VM.\\n   165\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"42n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   166\\t           (xl/call [:clojure\\n   167\\t                     \\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :customer :seal \\\\\\\"wax\\\\\\\" :marker 42} :marker))\\\"]\\n   168\\t                    [\\\"probe\\\"]\\n   169\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(probe());\\\"]))))\\n   170\\t  (testing \\\"a full-shape three-entry map with a valid-format 64-char seal is ordinary invocable data\\\"\\n   171\\t    ;; The exact issued format — three entries, a seal string of the issued\\n   172\\t    ;; length — with an :id the engine's heap never minted: the call site\\n   173\\t    ;; asks the heap (cell/authentic?), the heap does not authenticate the\\n   174\\t    ;; map, and the invocation is the map lookup answering the stored seal\\n   175\\t    ;; string, where the shape gates of the previous rounds routed it to\\n   176\\t    ;; admission and the dereference refused the VM.\\n   177\\t    (is (= {:js/out [(str \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\" (apply str (repeat 64 \\\"a\\\")) \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\")], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   178\\t           (xl/call [:clojure\\n   179\\t                     (str \\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :some-key \\\"\\n   180\\t                          \\\":seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\"} :seal))\\\")]\\n   181\\t                    [\\\"probe\\\"]\\n   182\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(probe());\\\"]))))\\n   183\\t  (testing \\\"the gate's collision literal: an :id in the heap's own language answers as data\\\"\\n   184\\t    ;; The r4 reviewer's literal — :id :cell-7, an id spelling the heap\\n   185\\t    ;; itself could have minted, with a well-formed but wrong seal. The\\n   186\\t    ;; ruling of record routes by the issuer's answer, not the id\\n   187\\t    ;; language: the heap does not authenticate it, so the lookup answers\\n   188\\t    ;; :cell-7 where r4's gate still handed it to the dereference and the\\n   189\\t    ;; VM aborted it as dead-or-forged.\\n   190\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\":cell-7\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   191\\t           (xl/call [:clojure\\n   192\\t                     (str \\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :cell-7 \\\"\\n   193\\t                          \\\":seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\"} :id))\\\")]\\n   194\\t                    [\\\"probe\\\"]\\n   195\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(probe());\\\"]))))\\n   196\\t  (testing \\\"a runtime-built full-shape map (assoc-constructed, not a bound literal) invokes as data\\\"\\n   197\\t    ;; The map is assembled by assoc at runtime, so no literal ever holds\\n   198\\t    ;; it; the shape test runs on the constructed value and the lookup\\n   199\\t    ;; still answers the stored seal string.\\n   200\\t    (is (= {:js/out [(str \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\" (apply str (repeat 64 \\\"a\\\")) \\\"\\\\\\\"\\\")], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   201\\t           (xl/call [:clojure\\n   202\\t                     (str \\\"(defn probe [] (let [m (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :type :cell-ref) \\\"\\n   203\\t                          \\\":id :some-key) \\\"\\n   204\\t                          \\\":seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\")] \\\"\\n   205\\t                          \\\"(m :seal)))\\\")]\\n   206\\t                    [\\\"probe\\\"]\\n   207\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(probe());\\\"]))))\\n   208\\t  (testing \\\"a runtime-built map with the forged cell-ref shape is ordinary invocable data\\\"\\n   209\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"42n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   210\\t           (xl/call [:clojure\\n   211\\t                     \\\"(defn probe [] (let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :customer :seal \\\\\\\"wax\\\\\\\" :marker 42}] (m :marker)))\\\"]\\n   212\\t                    [\\\"probe\\\"]\\n   213\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(probe());\\\"])))))\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t\\n   216\\t(deftest python-function-kind-of-in-typescript-test\\n   217\\t  (testing \\\"js/kind-of over a cell-backed foreign callable is :function\\\"\\n   218\\t    (is (= {:js/out [\\\"function\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   219\\t           (xl/call [:python \\\"def py_fn(x):\\\\n    return x + 1\\\\n\\\"]\\n   220\\t                    [\\\"py_fn\\\"]\\n   221\\t                    [:typescript \\\"console.log(typeof py_fn);\\\"])))))\\n   222\\t\\n   223\\t\\n   224\\t(deftest limits-test\\n   225\\t  (testing \\\"a PHP array returned to TS is an opaque handle, usable in PHP\\\"\\n   226\\t    (let [src \\\"<?php function phpfn($a = 7) { return $a === 7 ? [1, 2, 3] : count($a); }\\\"]\\n   227\\t      ;; the PHP int `count` returns reaches TS as an integer (`3n`), not a\\n   228\\t      ;; JS number: the two preludes keep their own number kinds\\n   229\\t      (is (= {:js/out [\\\"3n\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   230\\t             (xl/call [:php src]\\n   231\\t                      [\\\"phpfn\\\"]\\n   232\\t                      [:typescript \\\"const h = phpfn(); console.log(phpfn(h));\\\"])))))\\n   233\\t  (testing \\\"PHP null is neither JS null nor undefined\\\"\\n   234\\t    (let [src \\\"<?php function phpfn() { return null; }\\\"]\\n   235\\t      (is (= {:js/out [\\\"false false\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\n   236\\t             (xl/call [:php src]\\n   237\\t                      [\\\"phpfn\\\"]\\n   238\\t                      [:typescript\\n   239\\t                       \\\"const n = phpfn(); console.log(n === null, n === undefined);\\\"]))))))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1880,1948p'; rg -n 'php/throw|throwExpression|Throw|php/try|raise|frame-enter|frame-leave' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1660,1772p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1,240p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_13\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1880,1948p'; rg -n 'php/throw|throwExpression|Throw|php/try|raise|frame-enter|frame-leave' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1660,1772p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1,240p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"  1880\\t\\n  1881\\t(defn- leftmost-token-text\\n  1882\\t  \\\"The text of the first token under `n`.\\\"\\n  1883\\t  [ctx n]\\n  1884\\t  (if (p/token? n)\\n  1885\\t    (when-not (= \\\"\\\\\\\\\\\" (:text n)) (:text n))\\n  1886\\t    (some #(leftmost-token-text ctx %) (core/kids ctx n))))\\n  1887\\t\\n  1888\\t\\n  1889\\t(defn- catch-clause-node\\n  1890\\t  \\\"`(if matches (do bind body) rest)` for one `catch` clause over error `e`.\\\"\\n  1891\\t  [ctx e clause rest]\\n  1892\\t  (let [types (mapv #(str/lower-case (class-text ctx %))\\n  1893\\t                    (core/rules ctx clause \\\"qualifiedStaticTypeRef\\\"))\\n  1894\\t        var (some #(when (and (p/token? %) (= \\\"VarName\\\" (:type %))) (:text %))\\n  1895\\t                  (core/kids ctx clause))\\n  1896\\t        test (reduce (fn [acc t]\\n  1897\\t                       (u/if-node acc (u/lit true) (app* 'php/instance-of e (u/lit t))))\\n  1898\\t                     (u/lit false)\\n  1899\\t                     types)\\n  1900\\t        body (lower ctx (first (core/rules ctx clause \\\"blockStatement\\\")))]\\n  1901\\t    (u/if-node test\\n  1902\\t               (if var\\n  1903\\t                 (u/then (write-var ctx var e) body)\\n  1904\\t                 (u/then (app* 'php/delref e) body))\\n  1905\\t               rest)))\\n  1906\\t\\n  1907\\t\\n  1908\\t(defn- lower-try\\n  1909\\t  \\\"`try { } catch (T $e) { } finally { }`: `php/try` delivers the error to the\\n  1910\\t   catch clauses in order, an unmatched one is raised again; `php/try-finally`\\n  1911\\t   runs the finally block on every exit, escapes and errors included.\\\"\\n  1912\\t  [ctx n]\\n  1913\\t  (let [block (first (core/rules ctx n \\\"blockStatement\\\"))\\n  1914\\t        clauses (core/rules ctx n \\\"catchClause\\\")\\n  1915\\t        fin (first (core/rules ctx n \\\"finallyStatement\\\"))\\n  1916\\t        e (core/gen \\\"e\\\" n)\\n  1917\\t        mark (core/gen \\\"mk\\\" n)\\n  1918\\t        body (lower ctx block)\\n  1919\\t        guarded (if (seq clauses)\\n  1920\\t                  (u/let1 mark\\n  1921\\t                          (app* 'php/tmp-mark)\\n  1922\\t                          (app* 'php/try\\n  1923\\t                                (u/lam [] body)\\n  1924\\t                                (u/lam [e]\\n  1925\\t                                       (u/then (app* 'php/release-tmps (u/v mark))\\n  1926\\t                                               (reduce (fn [rest clause]\\n  1927\\t                                                         (catch-clause-node ctx (u/v e) clause rest))\\n  1928\\t                                                       (app* 'php/raise (u/v e))\\n  1929\\t                                                       (reverse clauses))))\\n  1930\\t                                (u/lam [] (u/lit :php/null))))\\n  1931\\t                  body)]\\n  1932\\t    (u/then (if fin\\n  1933\\t              (app* 'php/try-finally\\n  1934\\t                    (u/lam [] guarded)\\n  1935\\t                    (u/lam [(core/gen \\\"x\\\" n)]\\n  1936\\t                           (lower ctx (first (core/rules ctx fin \\\"blockStatement\\\")))))\\n  1937\\t              guarded)\\n  1938\\t            (u/lit :php/null))))\\n  1939\\t\\n  1940\\t\\n  1941\\t(defn- lower-match\\n  1942\\t  \\\"`match (e) { a, b => r, default => d }`: strict comparison in order, the\\n  1943\\t   default last, else `UnhandledMatchError`.\\\"\\n  1944\\t  [ctx n]\\n  1945\\t  (let [subject (first (core/rules ctx n \\\"expression\\\"))\\n  1946\\t        m (core/gen \\\"m\\\" n)\\n  1947\\t        items (core/rules ctx n \\\"matchItem\\\")\\n  1948\\t        default? (fn [item]\\n616:    :else (app* 'php/throw-error (u/lit \\\"Error\\\") (u/lit \\\"Using $this when not in object context\\\"))))\\n1302:      \\\"Throw\\\" (app* 'php/throw-value (lower ctx operand))\\n1909:  \\\"`try { } catch (T $e) { } finally { }`: `php/try` delivers the error to the\\n1910:   catch clauses in order, an unmatched one is raised again; `php/try-finally`\\n1922:                          (app* 'php/try\\n1928:                                                       (app* 'php/raise (u/v e))\\n1933:              (app* 'php/try-finally\\n1987:                   (app* 'php/throw-error\\n3204:                           (app* 'php/try-finally\\n3210:                   (app* 'php/try-finally\\n3600:    \\\"throwStatement\\\" (app* 'php/throw-value (lower ctx (first (core/rules ctx n \\\"expression\\\"))))\\n  1660\\t\\n  1661\\t(declare lower-try-except)\\n  1662\\t\\n  1663\\t\\n  1664\\t(defn- lower-try\\n  1665\\t  \\\"`try` with `except` clauses (`py/try`), with `finally` (`py/try-finally`\\n  1666\\t   around the rest), or both. The finally thunk takes the exception being\\n  1667\\t   raised through it, or None, and ignores it.\\\"\\n  1668\\t  [ctx n]\\n  1669\\t  (let [ks (kids ctx n)\\n  1670\\t        blocks (rules ctx n \\\"block\\\")]\\n  1671\\t    (if (some #(p/token? % \\\"finally\\\") ks)\\n  1672\\t      (app* 'py/try-finally\\n  1673\\t            (u/lam [] (if (seq (rules ctx n \\\"except_clause\\\"))\\n  1674\\t                        (lower-try-except ctx n (pop blocks))\\n  1675\\t                        (u/seq-nodes (lower-block ctx (first blocks)))))\\n  1676\\t            (u/lam [(gen \\\"fx\\\" n)] (u/seq-nodes (lower-block ctx (peek blocks)))))\\n  1677\\t      (lower-try-except ctx n blocks))))\\n  1678\\t\\n  1679\\t\\n  1680\\t(defn- lower-with\\n  1681\\t  \\\"`with a as x, b:` nests as `with a as x: with b:`; each item is\\n  1682\\t   `(py/with manager (fn [value] (assign target value) ...))`.\\\"\\n  1683\\t  [ctx n]\\n  1684\\t  (let [items (rules ctx n \\\"with_item\\\")\\n  1685\\t        body (u/seq-nodes (lower-block ctx (first (rules ctx n \\\"block\\\"))))]\\n  1686\\t    (reduce (fn [inner item]\\n  1687\\t              (let [ik (kids ctx item)\\n  1688\\t                    v (gen \\\"wv\\\" item)]\\n  1689\\t                (app* 'py/with\\n  1690\\t                      ((:lower ctx) ctx (first ik))\\n  1691\\t                      (u/lam [v]\\n  1692\\t                             (if (p/has-token? (:pk ctx) item \\\"as\\\")\\n  1693\\t                               (u/then (assign-target ctx (last ik) (u/v v)) inner)\\n  1694\\t                               inner)))))\\n  1695\\t            body\\n  1696\\t            (reverse items))))\\n  1697\\t\\n  1698\\t\\n  1699\\t(defn- lower-try-except\\n  1700\\t  \\\"`try` with `except` clauses and an optional `else`: `blocks` are the try\\n  1701\\t   body, one block per clause, then the else block if any.\\\"\\n  1702\\t  [ctx n blocks]\\n  1703\\t  (let [exc (gen \\\"exc\\\" n)\\n  1704\\t        clauses (rules ctx n \\\"except_clause\\\")\\n  1705\\t        body (u/seq-nodes (lower-block ctx (first blocks)))\\n  1706\\t        handler-blocks (subvec blocks 1 (inc (count clauses)))\\n  1707\\t        else-block (get blocks (inc (count clauses)))\\n  1708\\t        hctx (assoc ctx :exc exc)\\n  1709\\t        dispatch\\n  1710\\t        (reduce\\n  1711\\t          (fn [fallthrough [clause block]]\\n  1712\\t            (let [ck (kids ctx clause)\\n  1713\\t                  cls-node (first (rules ctx clause \\\"test\\\"))\\n  1714\\t                  as-name (first (rules ctx clause \\\"name\\\"))\\n  1715\\t                  handler (if as-name\\n  1716\\t                            ;; `except E as e:` binds e for the handler and\\n  1717\\t                            ;; unbinds it on every exit, as `del e` in a\\n  1718\\t                            ;; finally would\\n  1719\\t                            (let [nm (name-of ctx as-name)]\\n  1720\\t                              (app* 'py/try-finally\\n  1721\\t                                    (u/lam [] (u/seq-nodes\\n  1722\\t                                                (cons (assign-name ctx nm (u/v exc))\\n  1723\\t                                                      (lower-block hctx block))))\\n  1724\\t                                    (u/lam [(gen \\\"ux\\\" clause)] (unbind-name ctx nm))))\\n  1725\\t                            (u/seq-nodes (lower-block hctx block)))]\\n  1726\\t              (when (and (nil? cls-node) (> (count ck) 1))\\n  1727\\t                (unsupported! clause \\\"except clause\\\"))\\n  1728\\t              (if cls-node\\n  1729\\t                (u/if-node (app* 'py/exc-matches (u/v exc)\\n  1730\\t                                 ((:lower ctx) ctx cls-node))\\n  1731\\t                           handler\\n  1732\\t                           fallthrough)\\n  1733\\t                handler)))\\n  1734\\t          (app* 'py/raise (u/v exc))\\n  1735\\t          (reverse (map vector clauses handler-blocks)))]\\n  1736\\t    (app* 'py/try\\n  1737\\t          (u/lam [] body)\\n  1738\\t          (u/lam [exc] dispatch)\\n  1739\\t          (u/lam [] (if else-block\\n  1740\\t                      (u/seq-nodes (lower-block ctx else-block))\\n  1741\\t                      none)))))\\n  1742\\t\\n  1743\\t\\n  1744\\t(defn- lower-flow\\n  1745\\t  [ctx n]\\n  1746\\t  (case (:rule n)\\n  1747\\t    \\\"break_stmt\\\" (if-let [brk (get-in ctx [:loop :brk])]\\n  1748\\t                   (u/app (u/v brk) none)\\n  1749\\t                   (syntax! n \\\"'break' outside loop\\\"))\\n  1750\\t    \\\"continue_stmt\\\" (if (:loop ctx)\\n  1751\\t                      (u/app (u/v (get-in ctx [:loop :cont])) none)\\n  1752\\t                      (syntax! n \\\"'continue' not properly in loop\\\"))\\n  1753\\t    \\\"return_stmt\\\" (if-let [ret (:ret ctx)]\\n  1754\\t                    (u/app (u/v ret)\\n  1755\\t                           (if-let [value (first (rules ctx n \\\"testlist\\\"))]\\n  1756\\t                             (display ctx value)\\n  1757\\t                             none))\\n  1758\\t                    (syntax! n \\\"'return' outside function\\\"))\\n  1759\\t    \\\"raise_stmt\\\"\\n  1760\\t    (let [tests (rules ctx n \\\"test\\\")]\\n  1761\\t      (cond\\n  1762\\t        (p/has-token? (:pk ctx) n \\\"from\\\") (unsupported! n \\\"raise from\\\")\\n  1763\\t        (empty? tests) (if-let [exc (:exc ctx)]\\n  1764\\t                         (app* 'py/raise (u/v exc))\\n  1765\\t                         (unsupported! n \\\"bare raise outside except\\\"))\\n  1766\\t        :else (app* 'py/raise (app* 'py/as-exception\\n  1767\\t                                    ((:lower ctx) ctx (first tests))))))))\\n  1768\\t\\n  1769\\t\\n  1770\\t(def ^:private comprehension-names\\n  1771\\t  {:list \\\"list comprehension\\\", :set \\\"set comprehension\\\", :dict \\\"dict comprehension\\\",\\n  1772\\t   :genexp \\\"generator expression\\\"})\\n     1\\t(ns yang.clojure.prelude\\n     2\\t  \\\"The `clj` runtime module (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.10):\\n     3\\t   the published linker module every linked clojure program requires, as\\n     4\\t   `js`, `php` and `py` are for their frontends. It is written in prelude\\n     5\\t   notation and emitted with the same core machinery those preludes use;\\n     6\\t   it never runs on the host.\\n     7\\t\\n     8\\t   Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\t   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\\n    11\\t     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\\n    12\\t     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\\n    13\\t     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\\n    14\\t     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\\n    15\\t     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\\n    16\\t     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\\n    17\\t     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\\n    18\\t     standing);\\n    19\\t   - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\\n    20\\t     `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\\n    21\\t     allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\\n    22\\t     program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\\n    23\\t     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\\n    24\\t     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\\n    25\\t     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\\n    26\\t     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\\n    27\\t     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\\n    28\\t     module dictionary are the same seam;\\n    29\\t   - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\\n    30\\t     needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\\n    31\\t     adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\\n    32\\t     predicates read.\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t   The module pins the shared calling runtime (`yang.call`) at the\\n    35\\t   convention's call-address, as the other runtimes do, and refuses before\\n    36\\t   anything is published when a free name nothing supplies is read.\\\"\\n    37\\t  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\\n    38\\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\\n    39\\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n    40\\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\\n    41\\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t(def module-name\\n    45\\t  \\\"The linker module name of the clojure runtime.\\\"\\n    46\\t  'clj)\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t(def runtime-keys\\n    50\\t  \\\"Every runtime key, each with an `:clj/uninit` placeholder at module\\n    51\\t   level so every read is discharged before `clj/init!` allocates the\\n    52\\t   real cell. They stay qualified: internal store keys, never guest\\n    53\\t   names.\\\"\\n    54\\t  '[clj.rt/state clj.rt/globals])\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t(def definitions\\n    58\\t  \\\"The module's definition list, in prelude notation (the module's own\\n    59\\t   `clj/` prefix is stripped on emit).\\\"\\n    60\\t  '[;; ------------------------------------------------- state and namespace\\n    61\\t    [clj/init!\\n    62\\t     (fn []\\n    63\\t       (if (= clj.rt/state :clj/uninit)\\n    64\\t         (do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))\\n    65\\t             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/state) :clj/ready))\\n    66\\t         :clj/ready))]\\n    67\\t    ;; the runtime global namespace: one task-local map in a cell, keyed by\\n    68\\t    ;; export name. `clj/define-global!` answers the value, so a publish\\n    69\\t    ;; sequence can chain through it.\\n    70\\t    [clj/define-global!\\n    71\\t     (fn [name value]\\n    72\\t       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\\n    73\\t                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\\n    74\\t           value))]\\n    75\\t    [clj/global-get\\n    76\\t     (fn [name]\\n    77\\t       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\\n    78\\t         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\\n    79\\t         :clj/unbound))]\\n    80\\t\\n    81\\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- entry\\n    82\\t    ;; The outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper is frontend-\\n    83\\t    ;; internal, so the entry removes one wrapper level from the\\n    84\\t    ;; program's value (a program returning that vector as data was\\n    85\\t    ;; wrapped again, so one level is exact). An error outcome passes\\n    86\\t    ;; through as the failure value for the caller to render.\\n    87\\t    [clj/unwrap-outcome\\n    88\\t     (fn [value]\\n    89\\t       (if (if (data/vector? value) (= (data/count value) 2) false)\\n    90\\t         (if (= (data/nth value 0) :yin.k/ok)\\n    91\\t           (data/nth value 1)\\n    92\\t           value)\\n    93\\t         value))]\\n    94\\t    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\\n    95\\t    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\\n    96\\t    [clj/run-main\\n    97\\t     (fn [body]\\n    98\\t       (do (clj/init!)\\n    99\\t           (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\\n   100\\t\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\t(def module-definitions\\n   103\\t  \\\"The module's definition list: an `:clj/uninit` placeholder for every\\n   104\\t   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\\\"\\n   105\\t  (core/module-definitions \\\"clj\\\" :clj/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\\n   106\\t\\n   107\\t\\n   108\\t(def module-uast\\n   109\\t  \\\"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\\n   110\\t   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level.\\\"\\n   111\\t  (core/module-tree module-definitions []))\\n   112\\t\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\t(def module-exports\\n   115\\t  \\\"The module's exports: every `clj/` key of the definition list, stripped.\\\"\\n   116\\t  (core/exports \\\"clj\\\" definitions))\\n   117\\t\\n   118\\t\\n   119\\t(def ^:private module-free-names\\n   120\\t  \\\"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the host\\n   121\\t   exports its manifest must declare.\\\"\\n   122\\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\\n   123\\t\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t(defn module-spec\\n   126\\t  \\\"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `clj` over\\n   127\\t   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call`\\n   128\\t   module at `call-address` — the convention's call-address, as every\\n   129\\t   runtime's publication carries. A free name nothing supplies is refused\\n   130\\t   before anything is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\\\"\\n   131\\t  [registry call-address]\\n   132\\t  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\\n   133\\t                     :ast module-uast,\\n   134\\t                     :exports module-exports,\\n   135\\t                     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\\n   136\\t                     :free-names module-free-names,\\n   137\\t                     :skip? #(= \\\"yang.call\\\" (namespace %)),\\n   138\\t                     :registry registry,\\n   139\\t                     :message \\\"the clj module reads an undeclared name\\\",\\n   140\\t                     :refusal-ns \\\"yang.clojure\\\"}))\\n   141\\t\\n   142\\t\\n   143\\t(defn register-library-module\\n   144\\t  \\\"Return `registry` with host module `name` installed over `entries`\\n   145\\t   (`[export function]` pairs) at `arities`, each export pure.\\\"\\n   146\\t  [registry name entries arities]\\n   147\\t  (module/register-host-module\\n   148\\t    registry name\\n   149\\t    (into {} entries)\\n   150\\t    (into {} (map (fn [[op _]] [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\\n   151\\t          entries)))\\n   152\\t\\n   153\\t\\n   154\\t(defn admit\\n   155\\t  \\\"Return `registry` with the guest library's host surface installed: the\\n   156\\t   `kind` module and the `portable` adapters of the data exports the\\n   157\\t   collection predicates read (yang.clojure's `library-adapters`). A\\n   158\\t   linked clojure composition registers them beside the other runtimes'\\n   159\\t   registry surfaces; a composition without a clojure program reads none\\n   160\\t   of them.\\\"\\n   161\\t  [registry]\\n   162\\t  (let [portable (into {}\\n   163\\t                       (map (fn [[source _]]\\n   164\\t                              (let [op (symbol (name source))]\\n   165\\t                                [op (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\\n   166\\t                                                          (get data/data-module op))])))\\n   167\\t                       yang/library-adapters)]\\n   168\\t    (-> registry\\n   169\\t        (register-library-module 'kind yang/kind-module yang/kind-arities)\\n   170\\t        (register-library-module\\n   171\\t          'portable portable\\n   172\\t          (into {} (map (fn [op] [op 