e, a tagged two-element vector:\\n   622\\t;;\\n   623\\t;;   [:yin.k/ok value]       success; a LaTTe [:ok ...] stays an ordinary value\\n   624\\t;;   [:yin.k/error data]     failure; never a truthy return, only ever consumed\\n   625\\t;;                           by a call-site test or the harness boundary\\n   626\\t;;\\n   627\\t;; Lowering is a source-to-source pass over one function body, run before the\\n   628\\t;; ordinary compile. A tail form returns an outcome: a value is wrapped,\\n   629\\t;; and a source call is admitted before invoking the common entry. Generated\\n   630\\t;; entries can forward a private body's outcome directly in tail position;\\n   631\\t;; public entries convert value/raise through the caller bridge. This keeps\\n   632\\t;; named and mutual tail chains at constant depth. `throw` becomes the error\\n   633\\t;; outcome. A may-fail form in operand position is the early return pattern:\\n   634\\t;;\\n   635\\t;;   (let [o <outcome>] (if (error? o) o <rest of the function with (payload o)>))\\n   636\\t;;\\n   637\\t;; The failing branch returns the outcome in tail position. `ex-info` becomes\\n   638\\t;; a portable map under namespaced keys. A native primitive returns a raw\\n   639\\t;; value, except an adapted one (`:adapters`, source symbol to adapter symbol),\\n   640\\t;; whose host adapter already returns an outcome. Generated names carry the\\n   641\\t;; reserved `dsg__` prefix and bind through the internal `dsg__let`, which\\n   642\\t;; skips the user-binder check; the program pre-pass keeps user code out of\\n   643\\t;; that prefix. A macro call is opaque to the pass: the expander owns it.\\n   644\\t\\n   645\\t(def ^:private ok-tag :yin.k/ok)\\n   646\\t\\n   647\\t(def ^:private error-tag :yin.k/error)\\n   648\\t\\n   649\\t\\n   650\\t(defn- outcomes?\\n   651\\t  [env]\\n   652\\t  (some? (::outcomes env)))\\n   653\\t\\n   654\\t\\n   655\\t(defn- adapters\\n   656\\t  [env]\\n   657\\t  (:adapters (::outcome