{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3920,3935p;3960,4005p;4016,4076p;4105,4147p'; nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md\"","aggregated_output":"  3920\tprecedes B cleanup, which precedes outer A handling. Every activation\n  3921\towns its saved state and raise exit, without a single current-foreign-\n  3922\thandler cell or ambient dispatcher. Unchanged rethrow preserves the\n  3923\tinner exception as specified in section 8.10.7.\n  3924\t\n  3925\tCleanup runs once per actual exit. Resuming a suspended VM transition\n  3926\tmust not repeat parameter binding, argument evaluation, defaults,\n  3927\treference acquisition, or completed cleanup. The record, continuations,\n  3928\tand explicit runtime state use the existing continuation machinery and\n  3929\tits admission restrictions.\n  3930\t\n  3931\tA generator or asynchronous function returns its source-defined object.\n  3932\tSuspension on a stream effect keeps the activation; it is not a new\n  3933\tcall. A later generator resume or scheduled job has a new activation and\n  3934\tvalid bridge, never the raise exit of a call that already returned.\n  3935\tUnrestricted continuation escape across foreign frames is not implicitly\n  3960\tDo not duplicate existing lambda parameters in another persisted\n  3961\tauthority over the private body signature.\n  3962\t\n  3963\tBefore admitting a compiled composition, its profile/dependency\n  3964\tdeclarations must establish one compatible convention revision for the\n  3965\tentries it exposes. An incompatible revision needs an explicitly pinned\n  3966\tprojection or is refused before execution. Neither a common slot name nor\n  3967\tan opaque runtime closure proves revision compatibility. No runtime\n  3968\tlanguage registry or inspection of captured environments supplies it.\n  3969\t\n  3970\tChanged entry code changes code identities through the normal encoder.\n  3971\tRetain source, lowered UAST, pinned profiles, and projections under\n  3972\texisting provenance/unitarity rules. A fast path may omit the record\n  3973\tonly after proving equivalent evaluation, binding, foreign callability,\n  3974\texceptions, effects, suspension, and identity. Correctness must not\n  3975\tdepend on that optimization.\n  3976\t\n  3977\t#### 8.10.10 Current code and migration\n  3978\t\n  3979\tThe current code records the gap, not a second normative convention:\n  3980\t\n  3981\t| Current implementation | Private call path |\n  3982\t|---|---|\n  3983\t| `yang.python.antlr.prelude` | `py/call-kw` binds arguments and applies the function cell's `:code` to one vector. |\n  3984\t| `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` | `js/call` checks `:js/type :function` and applies `:code` to receiver and argument vector. |\n  3985\t| `yang.php.antlr.prelude` | `php/call` applies `:code` to the function cell and argument vector; named/reference handling is separate. |\n  3986\t| `test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj` | Demonstrates PHP/TypeScript substrate composition using lookup rewriting and a test-local `js-shaped` wrapper; not proof of this convention. |\n  3987\t\n  3988\tImplementation proceeds as separately verified changes:\n  3989\t\n  3990\t1. Supply the shared guest prelude and fixtures for entry discovery,\n  3991\t   record validation, and condition transfer, using existing bundled/\n  3992\t   linked prelude emitter machinery.\n  3993\t2. Add entries to each supported callable constructor and builtin;\n  3994\t   preserve source metadata/private code while putting binding and\n  3995\t   exception boundaries under the entry. Keep existing source `:call`\n  3996\t   safepoint marks on their original source activation, normally the\n  3997\t   private body; generated entry/binding boilerplate remains unmarked.\n  3998\t   Do not copy a body's source mark onto its entry and count both. A\n  3999\t   separately proved instrumentation transformation may relocate a mark\n  4000\t   only while preserving its source timing and exactly one activation.\n  4001\t3. Route source-resolved calls and callable tests through the convention,\n  4002\t   including supported bound methods, callable objects, recursion, and\n  4003\t   nested runtime re-entry.\n  4004\t4. Integrate explicit export/name projections with module publication\n  4005\t   and task-local instantiation; remove test-only language-pair wrappers\n  4016\t#### 8.10.11 Acceptance gates\n  4017\t\n  4018\tExecute real lowered source bodies, not only synthetic functions with\n  4019\tthe expected slot. A harness may compose published exports and namespace\n  4020\tprojections explicitly. It must not rewrite call nodes, extract foreign\n  4021\t`:code`, or insert test-local language-pair wrappers to make calls work.\n  4022\t\n  4023\tRequired evidence:\n  4024\t\n  4025\t- **Local semantics:** existing suites preserve argument order, defaults,\n  4026\t  required/extra arguments, keyword errors, receivers, exceptions, and\n  4027\t  supported reference/static behavior.\n  4028\t- **Direct calls:** each implemented frontend calls every other\n  4029\t  conforming frontend through the same mechanism in both directions\n  4030\t  with compatible values. Derive the test matrix from admitted\n  4031\t  frontends; do not hard-code it into runtime dispatch.\n  4032\t- **Higher-order calls:** pass, return, store, recurse, and call back\n  4033\t  through received functions. Assert identity and captures without\n  4034\t  replacement cells.\n  4035\t- **Callable admission:** source data with an entry-spelled property\n  4036\t  remains data; profile-constructed descriptors are admitted. Exercise\n  4037\t  supported PHP string/array designators both under local resolution and\n  4038\t  explicit callable export, preserving required late lookup without\n  4039\t  foreign namespace guessing.\n  4040\t- **Presence and binding:** distinguish missing from explicit\n  4041\t  null/None/undefined; retain duplicate keywords until binding; supply\n  4042\t  bound self once; evaluate receiver/spreads/defaults at source-defined\n  4043\t  times and counts.\n  4044\t- **Dynamic callability:** where supported, an existing instance becomes\n  4045\t  eligible after its class gains a call method and ineligible after\n  4046\t  deletion. Calls whose arguments change this metadata observe the\n  4047\t  correct source-required lookup time without instance rewrapping.\n  4048\t- **Opaque values:** round-trip foreign objects, functions, strings,\n  4049\t  float64 content, and exact integers unchanged. Assert aliasing and no\n  4050\t  silent rounding/null conversion. Unsupported operations yield\n  4051\t  documented guest errors.\n  4052\t- **References:** absent/incompatible writable-location profiles fail\n  4053\t  before reference acquisition and the body, with no reference-induced\n  4054\t  writeback. Source-required side effects from evaluating arguments still\n  4055\t  occur; rejection must not erase them. Compatible profiles prove\n  4056\t  mutation, aliasing, cleanup, and suspension behavior.\n  4057\t- **Exceptions:** cover binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\n  4058\t  catch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, replacement in `finally`,\n  4059\t  protocol-error rethrow, condition-shaped thrown maps, and A-to-B-to-A\n  4060\t  propagation. Assert original exception identity and cleanup order,\n  4061\t  not only rendered text. Store/return a generated `ForeignException`,\n  4062\t  finish its creating activation, then rethrow it from another activation\n  4063\t  and assert recovery of the original condition and payload identity.\n  4064\t- **Context lifetime:** repeated success/raise/success, cross-runtime\n  4065\t  recursion, and stream suspension/resume restore handler/depth/frame\n  4066\t  state and perform arguments/cleanup exactly once. Entry boilerplate\n  4067\t  must not double-count source recursion or tracing activations.\n  4068\t- **Publication/custody:** bundled/linked forms agree; two importing\n  4069\t  tasks have independent state. Existing gates still refuse foreign-task\n  4070\t  cells, forged refs, host functions, and inadmissible continuations.\n  4071\t- **Portability:** execute portable packet-to-UAST fixtures on JVM,\n  4072\t  Node, and Dart over the four VMs wherever existing contracts admit\n  4073\t  the program. JVM-only parsers may supply checked-in CST fixtures;\n  4074\t  parser availability is distinct from calling conformance.\n  4075\t\n  4076\tReport callable kinds, binding/value extensions, actual host/VM\n  4105\t  admission/apply machinery); not authentic → ordinary data semantics\n  4106\t  (map lookup). The shape remains a cheap pre-filter for WHEN to ask;\n  4107\t  it never decides meaning. The shared descriptor projection\n  4108\t  (`yang.call/_descriptor`) consults the same way.\n  4109\t- **Interim asymmetry (agreed across the four seats).** The frontend\n  4110\t  kind predicates that route on a `:type :cell-ref` tag before\n  4111\t  dereferencing — TypeScript's `js/cell?` and Python's `py/cell?` —\n  4112\t  still test SHAPE alone at this landing; their owning seats sweep\n  4113\t  them onto `cell/authentic?` in-lane after this merge (TypeScript:\n  4114\t  the `typeof` path and member-call lowering; Python: the three deref\n  4115\t  sites — `py/content-type`, type resolution, `py/eq-objects`). Until\n  4116\t  those sweeps land, a map imitating the reference language is data\n  4117\t  at Clojure positions and at the shared descriptor projection, but\n  4118\t  can still abort at the unswept frontend predicates. Nothing\n  4119\t  currently-correct changes behavior (the widening property holds);\n  4120\t  all-frontends consistency completes at the owning seats' landings.\n  4121\t- **Authentication is not authorization.** An authentic reference\n  4122\t  whose cell lacks an admitted callable entry is not callable; the\n  4123\t  existing not-callable refusal stands. Explicit dereference at a\n  4124\t  reference position (`cell/get`) likewise keeps the strict\n  4125\t  validation boundary — the data fallback lives in call routing.\n  4126\t- **Bearer policy.** An exact copy of a valid reference retains\n  4127\t  bearer behavior: it authenticates, therefore it resolves. No\n  4128\t  construction-history promises are made for identical values. A\n  4129\t  program wanting such a map's fields as data uses explicit lookup at\n  4130\t  a data position.\n  4131\t- **Bag clarification.** A reference stored in data remains a\n  4132\t  reference: storage changes nothing about the value, and what\n  4133\t  decides is the authentication query at the eventual call, not where\n  4134\t  the callee travelled. Equality survives while callability follows\n  4135\t  the heap's answer.\n  4136\t- **Entry-key exception.** \"Ordinary map application always remains\n  4137\t  data\" is true for the cell-ref language, not universally: a map\n  4138\t  carrying `:yang.call/entry` is convention territory whether it\n  4139\t  admits or forges one, and the D2 admission policy (the unadmitted\n  4140\t  entry-shaped map refuses) governs it. That policy is the one\n  4141\t  declared shape-routed exception and is unchanged by this ruling.\n  4142\t- **Static specialization** (a projected-name fast path, say)\n  4143\t  remains an optimization requiring proof of equivalence under\n  4144\t  shadowing and higher-order use, never the routing default: the\n  4145\t  calling contract's pass/return/store/recurse/callback obligations\n  4146\t  (8.10.11) bind every specialization.\n  4147\t\nnl: collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md; python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"collab/yang-python/1794900000000-reviewer-exception-uniformity-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\"; a=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p) if x.startswith(\\\"{\\\")]; m=[x[\\\"item\\\"][\\\"text\\\"] for x in a if x.get(\\\"item\\\",{}).get(\\\"type\\\")==\\\"agent_message\\\"]; print(m[-1])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/exception-track/1794920000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity.md; python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"collab/yang-python/1794900000000-reviewer-exception-uniformity-audit.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\"; a=[json.loads(x) for x in open(p) if x.startswith(\\\"{\\\")]; m=[x[\\\"item\\\"][\\\"text\\\"] for x in a if x.get(\\\"item\\\",{}).get(\\\"type\\\")==\\\"agent_message\\\"]; print(m[-1])'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-07 03:30:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-07 10:30:00 +07 (+0700)\n     3\tStatus: OWNER-APPROVED 2026-11-07 — \"enforce everywhere consistently. this should be a separate track.\"\n     4\t\n     5\t# RULING OF RECORD — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\n     6\t\n     7\t## The decision\n     8\t\n     9\tException handling is enforced uniformly across yang.clojure, yang.typescript (js),\n    10\tyang.php, and yang.python. Every escaping source exception — from any frontend, through\n    11\tany boundary — compiles down to THE SAME continuation: the caller's supplied raise exit\n    12\treceiving the §8.10.7 condition\n    13\t\n    14\t    {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original-thrown-value}\n    15\t\n    16\tand every receiving runtime implements the §8.10.7 reception rules (1)–(3) as written.\n    17\tThis is a SEPARATE TRACK: it does not ride any frontend's ongoing slice; it has its own\n    18\tfolder (`collab/exception-track/`), its own rounds, and its own acceptance gate. The four\n    19\tfrontend seats cede these exception-fix surfaces to the track's rounds; the track files\n    20\tper-frontend results back into each seat's records.\n    21\t\n    22\t## The uniformity requirements (each is testable)\n    23\t\n    24\t**R1 — the callee bridge (js, php are non-compliant today).** Every frontend's published\n    25\tfunction entry (and closure/higher-order entry) installs the exception bridge: it reads\n    26\tthe supplied `:yang.call/raise` and delivers every escaping source exception AND argument\n    27\tbinding failure to it as the §8.10.7 condition. No frontend may let an escaping exception\n    28\tfollow the host engine's own handler stack (js today, prelude.cljc:1581), and no frontend\n    29\tmay return an uncaught error as an ordinary value (php today, prelude.cljc:190/2384).\n    30\t\n    31\t**R2 — foreign reception (python, php are non-compliant today).** On receiving a thrown\n    32\tcondition: a payload valid in the receiving runtime keeps that runtime's ordinary\n    33\tcatching and identity behavior; a runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values (js) may\n    34\tdeliver the payload raw; a runtime requiring exception objects (python, php) represents a\n    35\tforeign payload with its own generated `ForeignException`, retaining the complete\n    36\tcondition and original payload — catch-all catches it, typed catches match the LOCAL\n    37\thierarchy, never guessed foreign class names. Raising the raw envelope (php:2384) or the\n    38\traw payload (python:1034) is non-compliant.\n    39\t\n    40\t**R3 — protocol failures retain the condition.** `:yang.call/not-callable`,\n    41\t`:invalid-invocation`, `:unsupported-binding` map to a documented local exception form\n    42\tretaining the complete original condition, so an unchanged rethrow can forward it. A fresh\n    43\tlocal error containing only rendered text (js:1627, python:1046) is non-compliant.\n    44\t\n    45\t**R4 — clojure unifies.** The internal outcome-token channel\n    46\t(clojure.cljc:1110/1486) may remain an optimization ONLY with a proof of equivalence at\n    47\tevery boundary; absent that proof it unifies onto the raise-exit path. Clojure's `try`\n    48\trejection of `finally` and its single-catch restriction are source-semantics decisions\n    49\tTHIS RULING DOES NOT CHANGE — R4 is about the continuation, not clojure's catch surface.\n    50\t\n    51\t**R5 — no new shape-routing.** Nothing in the track may route on the condition map's\n    52\tshape beyond the §8.10.7 contract; a lookalike map stays ordinary data (the cell-ref\n    53\truling's rule, restated). No synthesized engine-effect exception values.\n    54\t\n    55\t## What the audit establishes (the baseline)\n    56\t\n    57\tThe gpt-6.1-sol audit (collab/yang-python/1794900000000, verdict DIVERGENT, HEAD\n    58\te9a0b430) is the track's baseline evidence: python hooks the raise exit (R1 compliant);\n    59\tjs and php lack the bridge (R1); python and php lack ForeignException (R2); js and python\n    60\tlose protocol conditions (R3); clojure has the private channel (R4). Zero cross-language\n    61\t§8.10.7 legs exist in the conformance kit today.\n    62\t\n    63\t## Acceptance gate\n    64\t\n    65\tThe conformance kit (`test/yang/call/conformance.clj`) grows exception legs — the\n    66\t§8.10.11 exception row as acceptance: binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\n    67\tcatch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, finally replacement, protocol-error rethrow,\n    68\tcondition-shaped thrown maps staying data, A→B→A propagation with identity and cleanup\n    69\torder, and the stored-ForeignException rethrown-from-another-activation case. The track\n    70\tis DONE when every admitted pair passes those legs with real source on both sides, and\n    71\tthe divergences R1–R4 are each closed by a focused test pinning the compliant behavior.\n    72\t\n    73\t## Sequencing\n    74\t\n    75\tArchitect review of this ruling, then an engineer mob review, then per-frontend fix\n    76\trounds (smallest first: R3 js/python, R1 php, R2 python/php, R4 clojure), the conformance\n    77\tlegs landing alongside the fixes they gate. The known-gaps row for this track is filed\n    78\tfrom the audit's divergence list.\n    79\t\n    80\t— filed by the yang.python orchestrator seat on the owner's instruction\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-1zybYAb9' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-07 09:37:07.364 xcodebuild[13368:113774675]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-07 09:37:07.592 xcodebuild[13368:113774674] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\npython3: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\npython3: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-muGkzpAh' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-07 09:37:08.379 xcodebuild[13373:113774743]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-07 09:37:08.566 xcodebuild[13373:113774742] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\nThe “same continuation” claim is **false in this snapshot**. Clojure and Python connect fresh escaping exceptions to the supplied raise exit; JavaScript and PHP do not. Foreign reception and protocol-error rethrow also diverge.\n\nRead-only audit of `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12`, HEAD `e9a0b430`. No files edited; no tests run. Behavioral consequences below are static deductions from the code.\n\n**yang.clojure — DIVERGENT.**\n\n- **Lowering:** `throw` becomes `[:yin.k/error payload]`. `try` examines that outcome and binds its payload to the handler. It accepts exactly one `Exception`/`ExceptionInfo` catch, performs no runtime class discrimination, and rejects `finally`. See [clojure.cljc:904](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:904).\n- **Raise-exit hookup:** the public entry reads `:yang.call/raise` at line 1070 and invokes it with `(yang.call/thrown payload)` at [clojure.cljc:1088](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1088). Fresh public escapes therefore have the specified condition shape.\n- **Private path:** intra-unit calls pass `[compiler-token args]` and receive outcomes directly; authenticated outcome-token calls also bypass public value/raise conversion. See [clojure.cljc:1110](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1110), [clojure.cljc:1486](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1486). Thus its internal exception lowering is an ordinary result channel, unlike the other frontends’ handler continuations.\n- **Foreign reception:** `compile-guest-call` supplies a capture-backed raise closure. A delivered `:yang.call/thrown` becomes an error outcome containing the **raw payload**; another reason becomes an error outcome containing the **whole condition as data**. See [clojure.cljc:1297](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1297). Source catches receive that data. Rethrowing a protocol condition subsequently reaches the public entry’s unconditional `yang.call/thrown`, changing its reason rather than forwarding the original condition.\n- **Root:** `clj/run-main` unwraps successful outcomes and leaves error outcomes as reporting values; it supplies no invocation raise exit. See [clojure/prelude.cljc:87](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc:87).\n\n**yang.typescript / JavaScript — DIVERGENT.**\n\n- **Lowering:** `throw` calls `js/throw`; `try/catch` calls `js/try`; an enclosing `finally` calls `js/try-finally`. See [lower.cljc:2165](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc:2165), line 2214.\n- **Local continuation:** `js/try` captures a guest continuation and installs it in `js.rt/ctx`; `js/throw` walks that runtime’s handler/finally stack. These are guest continuations, not host-native `try/catch`. See [prelude.cljc:1704](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1704).\n- **Raise-exit hookup: absent for escaping source exceptions.** The published function entry directly applies `:code`; it neither reads `:yang.call/raise` nor installs a per-activation exception bridge. See [prelude.cljc:1581](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1581). An escaping throw therefore follows existing JS handlers rather than the foreign caller’s supplied exit. With no JS handler, it reaches the `:js/no-handler` expression.\n- **Foreign reception:** `js/call` really does deliver `:yang.call/value` raw through `js/throw`. However, protocol failures become newly constructed `TypeError`s containing only selected text; the original condition is discarded. See [prelude.cljc:1627](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1627). Unchanged protocol-error rethrow cannot recover it.\n- **Root:** `js/run-main` installs a JS root handler and snapshots uncaught values; it does not repair the missing callee bridge. See [prelude.cljc:1850](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc:1850).\n\n**yang.php — DIVERGENT.**\n\n- **Lowering:** source throws call `php/throw-value`; catches dispatch through local `php/instance-of`; unmatched catches call `php/raise`; `finally` becomes `php/try-finally`. See [lower.cljc:1889](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:1889), line 3600. `throw-value` requires a local Throwable and then raises it. See [prelude.cljc:4084](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4084).\n- **Local continuation:** `php/try` captures a guest handler continuation; `php/raise` walks PHP’s handler/finally stack. With an empty stack, `php/raise` **returns the error normally**. See [prelude.cljc:190](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:190).\n- **Raise-exit hookup: absent for source/binding exceptions.** The function entry performs named-argument placement and applies `:code` without an exception bridge. Its supplied raise exit is used only for unsupported binding profiles. See [prelude.cljc:2264](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2264), line 2281. The Closure entry likewise ignores the supplied exit and delegates through `php/call`: [prelude.cljc:4217](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:4217).\n- **Foreign reception:** `php/call`, `call-with-binding-profile`, and `call-named` convert not-callable to a fresh local `Error`; otherwise they call **`php/raise condition`**, without extracting `:yang.call/value`. See [prelude.cljc:2384](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2384), line 4314. Even an original PHP Throwable arriving inside a valid thrown condition is therefore delivered as its envelope, not restored.\n- **`ForeignException`: nowhere.** No wrapper, local hierarchy, or identity-owned retained-condition association exists. `catch (Throwable)` receives no valid local wrapper; explicitly throwing the envelope cannot preserve the original condition.\n- **Root:** `php/run-main` catches through PHP’s local stack and snapshots the result. See [prelude.cljc:5070](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5070).\n\n**yang.python — DIVERGENT.**\n\n- **Lowering:** `raise X` calls `py/as-exception` then `py/raise`; bare rethrow uses the captured exception directly. Typed clauses use `py/exc-matches`, bare `except` selects its handler unconditionally, and `finally` becomes `py/try-finally`. See [lower.cljc:1664](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1664), lines 1699 and 1759.\n- **Local continuation:** `py/try` captures and installs a guest handler, restoring saved context before calling its handler; `py/raise` runs intervening finally frames. See [prelude.cljc:294](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:294).\n- **Raise-exit hookup: present.** `py/function-entry` reads the supplied exit at line 893 and places **both argument binding and body execution** inside `py/try`. Its handler invokes that exit with the required `:yang.call/thrown`/`:yang.call/value` condition. See [prelude.cljc:886](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:886), line 912. Fresh escaping Python exceptions and binding failures follow the intended boundary path.\n- **Foreign reception:** `py/call-kw` delivers every thrown payload directly through `py/raise`, without validating whether it is a local exception or wrapping foreign data. Protocol failures become a generic `TypeError`, losing the condition. See [prelude.cljc:1034](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1034).\n- **`ForeignException`: nowhere.** Bare `except` can receive raw foreign data, but typed catches use `py/type-of` and the local hierarchy; foreign data has no generated local exception class. Explicit `raise e` applies `py/as-exception` and can replace that foreign payload with a `TypeError`. See [prelude.cljc:352](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:352), lines 754 and 802. There is no wrapper-lifetime condition association to recover in another activation.\n- **Root:** `py/run-main` catches and snapshots through Python’s local stack. See [prelude.cljc:3322](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:3322).\n\n**Local coverage inventory — assertions present, not rerun.**\n\n| Frontend | What its own tests pin |\n|---|---|\n| Clojure | Throw/error outcomes: [clojure_test.clj:1162](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1162). Broad admitted catch, nested replacement throw, operand escape, and rejection of `finally`/`Throwable`: [line 2452](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2452). Named binding failure emits `:yang.call/thrown`: line 1429. No unchanged-rethrow identity assertion found in these cases. |\n| JavaScript | Object and primitive throws, catch-all, finally on normal/return exits, string rethrow, uncaught exceptions: [e2e_test.clj:254](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/typescript/antlr/e2e_test.clj:254). Finally ordering/escape cleanup: [prelude_parity_test.cljc:677](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc:677), line 785. Typed catch syntax is inapplicable. |\n| PHP | Throwable hierarchy, typed/multi-type catches, `Throwable` catch-all, unmatched propagation, rethrow, finally/return override and exception replacement: [exceptions_test.clj:19](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/php/antlr/exceptions_test.clj:19), lines 33, 48 and 63. The test labelled “rethrow keeps the same object” checks its message, **not object identity**. |\n| Python | Typed catches across a local callee, bare rethrow, uncaught errors: [e2e_test.clj:534](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj:534), lines 554 and 609. Bare catch-all lowering: [lower_test.clj:197](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj:197). Finally on every exit, nested cleanup, return override and replacement exception: [e2e_c1_test.clj:30](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c1_test.clj:30), lines 62 and 91. Binder condition shape: [call_entry_test.cljc:76](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/python/antlr/call_entry_test.cljc:76). |\n\n**Cross-language evidence: the “zero exception legs” report is confirmed for the checked-in conformance tests.**\n\nThe shared kit composes donor exports and runs caller source; it contains no exception scenario itself: [conformance.clj:245](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/call/conformance.clj:245). Its real-source consumers in [cross_lang_test.clj:26](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj:26), Python’s [source_call_test.clj:9](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/python/antlr/source_call_test.clj:9), and TS/PHP’s [source_call_test.cljc:98](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call_test.cljc:98) exercise successful calls, callbacks, identity and opaque values—not escaping exceptions.\n\nThere **is** a JavaScript reception fixture asserting payload identity after a hand-built entry invokes the supplied raise exit: [prelude_parity_test.cljc:768](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc:768). That is useful helper evidence, but no second frontend compiles the throw. Likewise, shared helper tests construct conditions directly: [call_test.cljc:157](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-f12/test/yang/core/call_test.cljc:157).\n\nConsequently, no real-source language pair currently establishes the §8.10.7 propagation contract, including binding-failure propagation, foreign typed/catch-all reception, unchanged/protocol rethrow, finally replacement, A→B→A cleanup and identity, or saved `ForeignException` rethrow from another activation.\n\n**Ranked divergences:**\n\n1. **Missing callee exception bridges in JavaScript and PHP.** Their entries bypass the supplied raise exit for source exceptions; PHP binding failures also occur outside such a bridge. Evidence: JS prelude line 1581; PHP prelude lines 2264 and 4217.\n2. **Missing foreign-exception reception in Python and PHP.** Python raises raw foreign payloads; PHP raises the entire condition envelope. Neither implements `ForeignException` or its lifetime-owned condition association. Evidence: Python prelude line 1034; PHP prelude line 2384.\n3. **Original protocol conditions do not survive unchanged rethrow.** JS/Python discard them while constructing local errors; Clojure retains them as catch data but wraps a rethrow in a new thrown condition; PHP supplies an envelope without a valid local wrapper. Evidence: JS line 1634; Python line 1046; Clojure lines 1306 and 1088; PHP lines 2391 and 4085.\n4. **Clojure has a distinct internal failure channel and restricted catch/finally lowering.** Error vectors and authenticated private calls carry failures as ordinary results before public conversion. Evidence: compiler lines 904, 1110 and 1486.\n\nI found no synthesized engine-effect exception value, guessed foreign class-name matching, or source-map detector that forwards data merely because it looks like a condition. Dispatch on the reason of an actually delivered boundary condition is distinct from that forbidden shape inference.\n\n**Overall verdict: DIVERGENT.**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
